BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5726ec1ff7f83a78ad0dfe6b9c96de926e09dfc75ba72cd77c5c38278fcfa7ca@pruts-
 agenda.local
DTSTAMP:20260802T154420Z
SUMMARY:Echoes from Afar: Build your own archive
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20260912T120000Z
DTEND:20260912T140000Z
DESCRIPTION:Over the past years we’ve seen an increase in censorship\, sh
 adow-banning\, and blocking of accounts across large social media platform
 s like Instagram. Many artists\, designers\, and cultural and social organ
 isations\, rely on these platforms to connect with their communities and s
 hare their stories and their work. But what if we can build our own archiv
 es and websites\, and create our own networks to share our stories\, as a 
 way to keep authorship and intention in our own hands? \n\n\nThis hybird w
 orkshop\, led by Kexin Hong and Yiyao Wei\, opens through an introduction 
 to Echoes from Afar\, an open-source\, living\, online archive that explor
 es how digital infrastructures can challenge conventional forms of represe
 ntation while opening up space for Asian diasporic communities to narrate 
 their own stories. In its approach to storytelling\, the project seeks to 
 safeguard the integrity of personal narratives\, to cultivate plurality an
 d openness in how stories surface and circulate\, and to lay the groundwor
 k for a living archive that makes space for richer\, more textured forms o
 f visibility in the place of flattened or reductive images. \n\n\nIn the f
 irst part of the workshop\, participants will learn about Echoes from Afar
  and the basics of self-uploading and managing artworks on the platform\, 
 so that participants can begin contributing their own work if they would l
 ike to. In the second part of the workshop\, we will learn about the open-
 source workflow behind the archive\, showing how participants can build th
 eir own websites or archives using free and accessible tools that require 
 no prior coding experience. Throughout this hands-on process\, the worksho
 p will draw on AI technologies\, such as Claude\, as one of the working to
 ols that can assist website building\, while still remaining grounded in a
  practice of ethical care. \n\n\nNo prior coding experience is necessary a
 nd you do not need to be of Asian heritage to join this workshop. \n\n\nTh
 e Hmm experiments…\n\n\nThis event is part of a series of programs that 
 we are developing with The Hmm\, where we give space in our studio for our
  community to explore new ideas and experiment with workshops as part of o
 ur public program. \n\n\nWhat you need to know\n\n📅 Date: Saturday 12 S
 eptember 2026\n🕗 Times: 14.00 – 16.00 CEST\n📍 Location: The Hmm’
 s studio\, NDSM-plein 125\, 1033 WC Amsterdam\, and online\n🎟 Tickets: 
 €12\,50 regular\, €9\,50 students (onsite or online)\n\nAs these works
 hops are more intimate sessions\, there is a limited supply of tickets ava
 ilable. You can find information about physical accessibility at The Hmm
 ’s studio here. \n\n💚 This programme is kindly supported by the Crea
 tive Industries Fund NL
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/echoes-from-afar-build-your-own-archive/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
